 outside his  door he turned into jesse's classroom  his gun  either jammed or ran out of bullets and  during the short delay jesse called for  his friends to run and he's literally  credited with saving nine of  their lives and so i'm sitting on the  stand and i'm thinking you know in  comparison to what jesse did  this is the easier job for sure  safeguarding truth in our country  my attorney literally asked the jury to  choose love over fear and hatred and  they did yeah you mentioned uh choose  love in that movement which is a  non-profit that you founded in jesse's  name what do you hope people take away  from that  i hope that they take away the  uh fact that our personal power as human  beings is in our ability to choose in  any moment how we thoughtfully respond  and responding with love  is the powerful choice it feel good it  feels good and it's going to lead to a  safer more peaceful and loving world and  it's all of our choices every single day  from the moment we wake up scarlett i'm  in our view honestly because i just  think i'm still haunted by as we all are  haunted by that day at sandy hook how  you're able to talk so  um  comfortably about this such boys with  such such poise and such grace  considering it had to be one of the  worst moments of your life  well how are you able to do this a  message that my six-year-old son left on  our kitchen chalkboard  is really the reason he wrote three  words nurturing healing love  and it's six years old at six years old  phonetically spelled yeah because he was  in first grade and just learning to  write yes but i knew that that was a  spiritual awareness that he had that he  wasn't going to be on earth for very  much longer  it was a message of comfort for his  family and friends but also inspiration  it's where we needed to turn in order to  survive and thrive gail was asking how  you deal and how you heal  um  we are in  terrible times i'll just call it what it  is seems like we're talking about  a mass 